{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>But jackals shall rest — desert beasts.</b> They are animals that dwell in a desert land." "<b>Ostriches [ochim].</b> It has no [etymological] brother (root), and they are animals that astound all who see them." "<b>Daughters of the ostrich.</b> Well known, and they are birds." "<b>And goat-demons.</b> Like the form of demons (shedim), and they are hairy goats." "And it is possible that ochim are birds, and this is the correct view."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:40.343756006Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}